         14+'s full-access API (EKAuthorizationStatus.fullAccess) reads the
         Full key, while EKEventStore falls back to the legacy Write key on
         13.x, Flow's own LSMinimumSystemVersion floor. Without both, calling
         requestFullAccessToEvents on 13.x crashes instead of prompting. -->
    <key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Flow shows your calendar events alongside your tasks. Access is read-only — Flow never creates, edits, or deletes anything in your calendar.</string>
